<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">3 Effective Apr 01, 19, the Group has adopted Ind AS 116  Leases , applied to all lease contracts existing on Apr 01, 19 using the modified retrospective method which has resulted in recognition of right-of-use assets &amp; lease liabilities of Rs. 357.78 Lac in standalone financials &amp; Rs. 1052.64 Lac in consolidated financials as on transition date. The effect of this adoption is insignificant for the period.tttttt  n4 Exceptional items in the consolidated financial results include the following :tt  n a. Group's share of warranty provision recorded by Rane NSK Steering Systems P. Ltd (RNSS), a joint venture, amounting to Rs.808.50 Lac &amp; Rs.5,123.44 Lac for the quarter &amp; year ended Mar 31, 20 respectively towards incremental warranty claims with respect to certain specific lots of products sold by RNSS to one of its customers. These amounts have been determined by the management of the RNSS based on technical estimates, which is net of claims received from the customer against such warranty obligations. The corresponding figures for the quarter ended Dec 31, 2019, quarter &amp; year ended Mar 31, 19, amounted to Rs.1,776.74 Lac, Rs.392.00 Lac &amp; Rs.1,533.70 Lac respectively. ttttttttt  nb. VRS expenditure incurred by Rane Brake Lining Ltd (RBL), a subsidiary company, amounting to Rs. 91.40 Lac for the year ended Mar 31, 19.ttttt  nc. The Co./ Group has assessed the recoverable value of total investment, loans &amp; other financial assets held by Rane Madras Ltd (RML), a subsidiary, in its operating step down subsidiary (either directly or through an intermediate subsidiary) &amp; provided for an impairment of Rs. 3,757 Lac in the standalone financial statements of RML &amp; Rs.196 Lac in the consolidated financial statements of the group. The impact on the consolidated financial statements of the group has been disclosed as an exceptional items for the quarter &amp; year ended Mar 31, 20. In order to carry out the above assessment, projections of future cash flows based on the most recent long-term forecasts, including selling price as well as volumes are estimated over the next five years. The estimation of sales volumes is based on the management's assessment of probability of securing new businesses in the future, adverse business impact &amp; uncertainties arising due to COVID-19 pandemic to the extent known. The impact of COVID-19 on the Company’s/Group's financial results may differ from that estimated as at the date of approval of these financial results dependent on circumstances that evolve in the future.tttttttttt  n5  During the quarter ended Dec 31, 19, 17,42,160 warrants convertible into equity shares of Rs. 10/- each were issued &amp; allotted on preferential basis by RML out of which 580,720 warrants were converted into equity shares in Mar, 20. tttttttttt  n  n6 Pursuant to the Taxation Laws (Amendment) Ordinance, 19 issued on Sep 20, 19, corporate assessee have been given an option to apply a lower income tax rate with effect from Apr 01, 19, subject to certain conditions specified therein. Accordingly the company has opted to avail lower income tax rate with effect from Apr 01, 19 &amp; considered the same in the Standalone Financial results. However some of its entities in the group based on the evaluation of comparative tax costs &amp; considering the future performance forecasts, have not opted for the above said option, &amp; accordingly, no effect in this regard has presently been considered in the measurement of tax expense for the quarter &amp; year ended Mar 31, 2020 &amp; the consequent impact in the deferred tax as on that date to the consolidated results for those entities.tttttttttttttttttttt  n7 During the year the BOD had declared an Interim dividend of Rs.4 per share on Feb 10, 20 &amp; the same was paid on Feb 26, 20 &amp; recommended a final dividend of Rs.4 per equity share for FY 19-20.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
